    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0104" n="16" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg16"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Richardson to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 226.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In response to your dispatch of September
                    23, requesting copies of the neutrality proclamation issued by the Brazilian
                    Government, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of the one issued at the
                    beginning of the war between the United States and Spain,<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d15-f1"/> Brazil having issued no special proclamation for the
                    present war between Russia and Japan, as will be seen from the translation of
                    the note received with this, below.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles
                    Richardson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d15-a1.xml" xpointer="d15-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
